# ============================================================
# Activity Weather – Root Environment Variables
# ============================================================
# All variables must be prefixed with VITE_ to be picked up by Vite.
# ============================================================
#
# Frontend-only variables:
#
#   VITE_STORMGLASS_API_KEY=your_stormglass_api_key_here
#
# To configure the backend, copy server/.env.example to server/.env
# and fill in your values:
#
#   cp server/.env.example server/.env
#
# Required backend variables (see server/.env.example for full details):
#
#   STORMGLASS_API_KEY=your_stormglass_api_key_here
#   PORT=3001
#   DB_PATH=./data/activity-weather.sqlite
#
# Frontend proxy / preview overrides (optional):
#
#   VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:3001
#     Base URL for the /api proxy in `vite dev`. Set this to your
#     backend address (e.g. http://my-server.tailXXXXX.ts.net:3001)
#     so every installed instance can choose its own backend host.
#
#   VITE_PREVIEW_HOSTS=your-server.tailXXXXX.ts.net
#     Comma-separated hosts allowed by `vite preview`. Leave empty
#     to restrict to localhost-only.
#
#   VITE_HMR_HOST=your-server.tailXXXXX.ts.net
#     Forces the HMR websocket to reconnect to this host instead of
#     localhost. Required when accessing the dev server from inside
#     the container or from a Tailscale address.
# ============================================================
